# tts-flow_lm-90m-amh-3242h-v1.0

Amharic text-to-speech with voice cloning that runs on a CPU about 2x faster than real time. It is
[Kyutai Pocket TTS](https://github.com/kyutai-labs/pocket-tts) fine-tuned on Amharic, then distilled to 6 layers
(~100M parameters, 0.44 GB).

## Use

```bash
python tts_small_infer.py --text "ሰላም ጤና ይስጥልኝ። ዛሬ ስለ ኢትዮጵያ ዜና እንነጋገራለን።" --out out.wav --int8 [--voice ref.wav]
```

```python
from tts_small_infer import AmharicTTS
tts = AmharicTTS(threads=4, int8=True)
wav = tts.synth("ሰላም ጤና ይስጥልኝ።", voice="ref.wav")   # float32 numpy at tts.sample_rate (24000)
```

- **Voice:** a clean 3-5 s clip of one speaker; no transcript needed. Without one, `voices/default.wav` is used
  (a news-reader clip from the training data).
- **Text:** Amharic in Ethiopic script. Each sentence (split on ። ? !) is generated separately. Spell out numbers;
  Latin script is read poorly.
- **Needs:** `pocket-tts` (tested: git v4.0.1-19-gee2ebc8; the PyPI 4.0.1 wheel is untested), `torch`, `sentencepiece`, `pyyaml`, `numpy`, `soundfile`; `torchao` for
  `--int8`. Peak RAM about 1.7 GB.

## Quality

CER is measured with amharic-ctc v0.3, letters folded, spaces and punctuation ignored. The same 5 held-out voices are
used for every model.

| | clean100 CER | 162-set CER | speaker sim (clean100) |
|---|---|---|---|
| this model, as shipped (CPU, `tts_small_infer.py`, int8 / fp32) | 0.053 / 0.061 | | |
| this model (6 layers), GPU research eval | 0.074 | 0.112 | 0.952 |
| 24-layer teacher | 0.084 | 0.107 | |
| Amharic OmniVoice (GPU model) | 0.047 | 0.100 | 0.961 |
| real recordings | | 0.236 | |

- **clean100** is 100 held-out human-edited written sentences.
- **162-set** texts are ASR transcripts with errors, so every CER there is inflated.

**Speed:** on 4 CPU cores, RTF is 0.55 in fp32 and 0.53 in int8 (seconds of compute per
second of audio). This was measured on ARM cores of a shared machine.

## Training

- **Fine-tune:** the English 24-layer teacher, with a new sentencepiece text embedding.
  - Steps 0-5k: 964 h of Amharic news.
  - Steps 5k-15k: 1,593 h of news and podcasts.
  - 2.5k polish steps at lr 5e-5 on 415 h of the cleanest clips.
- **Data:** clips were filtered by agreement between the corpus transcript and amharic-ctc (CER <= 0.15, 0.05 for
  polish), with forced word alignment.
- **Distillation:** to 6 layers, with guidance (cfg 2.0) baked in.

